{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528928-opinion-the-fall-of-london-is-a-great-adventure-but-you-need-to-use-only-70-of-it","id":1528928,"title":"[Opinion] The Fall of London is a great adventure but you need to use only 70% of it","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-19T09:01:25-08:00","id":1528928,"title":"[Opinion] The Fall of London is a great adventure but you need to use only 70% of it","content":"The Fall of London gets quite a bit of (deserved) criticism. I think it's very dissonant with the rest of the line of V5. Basically, after the corebook and other material going to such elaborate lengths to stress personal horror, local play, high generation, lack of Elders, and keeping it &quot;real.&quot; Well, then you're on a mission to find a 4th generation vampire's horocruxes to restore him to absolute power.<br /> <br /> In a very real way, the module is a dungeon crawl. You travel across London as the Second Inquisition gets stronger and stronger until you make it to the final boss and decide whether to side with Mithras, against Mithras, or skip town.<br /> <br /> Except, honestly, I think there's a lot of solid material here that deserves to be appreciated. I do feel like the game as presented isn't a great introduction to V5 and needs some heavy modification to be as enjoyable as it could be. I've also run it twice with heavy modification and enjoyed the hell out of the resulting chronicles.<br /> <br /> Some suggestions from my area:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>The Player Characters can be original</b>: The game's pregens aren't necessary, IMHO. The way I ran it is the PCs are contacted by Mithras representative and offered FABULOUS REWARDS to retrieve the items in question. Which should be enough by itself to get the PCs involved. Once the PCs agree, you can even reveal they've been geased into finishing the quest but that probably isn't necessary.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Emphasize the Rising Tension</b>: The game starts with the Camarilla at its strongest in an ancient city with unassailable (seeming) power. Having it slowly change over the course of a week<br /> to a city under siege with most of the city's vampires destroyed or fled is something that does a better job of making the SI look interesting than the corebook.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>The Flashbacks to relay Mithras' backstory</b>: A lot of players have no idea who Mithras ir or why they should care. Since, again, they're basically horocruxes, you can use them to do flashbacks for the player characters holding them. Explain who Mithras is and why they should care about this vampire impersonating an ancient Middle Eastern god that was popular in Rome.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Gradually turn the player characters against everyone</b>: The important thing to remember in this module is everyone sucks. Mithras is the guy who brought the SI down on London's Kindred, Queen Anne is a Camarilla stooge/cannibal, the SI is self-obviously awdul, and there's no viable Anarch or Sabbat alternative. At the end, the PCs should be running their own scheme to either betray their employers or get PAID. If they're not plotting a double cross against Mithras with a fake horocrux or calling the SI down on everyone then they're not ambitious enough.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>Let them find out the Behind the Scenes Machines</b>: Making the SI seem invincible is fun but you can also have the slow drawning realization they're only succeeding because its leaders are members of the Cult of Mithras and being aided by the god vampire opening the front door for them. It should help them understand how deep the Jyhad goes as well as how little loyalty vampires have to one another.<br /> <br /> 6. <b>Let them Reap the Rewards</b>: When the dust settles, the PCs should have the alliance with some powerful figures in the world and be rewarded for it. Not because betrayal is unexpected in this world but because betrayal is rewarded.<br /> <br /> 7. <b>Throw in some Anarchs</b>: Because it's fucking London people and you're not going to have Anarchs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T12:11:44-08:00","id":1528942,"title":"","content":"That could work on why my player character might go back to London after a 100+ years of absence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T21:00:02-08:00","id":1528982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528928-opinion-the-fall-of-london-is-a-great-adventure-but-you-need-to-use-only-70-of-it#post1528928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fall of London gets quite a bit of (deserved) criticism. I think it's very dissonant with the rest of the line of V5. Basically, after the corebook and other material going to such elaborate lengths to stress personal horror, local play, high generation, lack of Elders, and keeping it &quot;real.&quot; Well, then you're on a mission to find a 4th generation vampire's horocruxes to restore him to absolute power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the matter is that, well, Fall of London from a canon/lore perspective is not quite a V5 story - it's pretty much a milestone event leading from V20 to V5, it's the bridge that marks the path between eras/editions through its burning. It's own concept makes it fitting with V5 somewhat problematic due to its &quot;major/trendsetting event&quot; nature and scale - and that even <b>before</b> we consider the whole &quot;city court going in flames&quot; trainwreck is part of some massive gonzo flex of Mithras against Lady Anne, Monty Coven (being on his body notwithstanding) <b><i>or both</i></b> while sending the PCs to gather his horcruxes twist reveal at the core of the adventure.<br /> <br /> Yes, it's complicated. I can understand the appeal of inserting the PCs into a milestone event of the setting or that marks the passage between editions - Last Supper started a whole trend in the game with this - but for a number of reasons dealing with London and its fall might not have been the best pick from a tone perspective. Or the real problem is writers deciding to make it all about Mithras <b><i>again</i></b> instead of giving us a more expansive view of the city and its kindred right before everything goes into the flames. Because &quot;there's a crazed meth pulling the strings&quot; does <b>not</b> really help with selling the SI as the evolved and matured antagonist organization/movement they are supposed to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528928-opinion-the-fall-of-london-is-a-great-adventure-but-you-need-to-use-only-70-of-it#post1528928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a very real way, the module is a dungeon crawl. You travel across London as the Second Inquisition gets stronger and stronger until you make it to the final boss and decide whether to side with Mithras, against Mithras, or skip town.<br /> <br /> Except, honestly, I think there's a lot of solid material here that deserves to be appreciated. I do feel like the game as presented isn't a great introduction to V5 and needs some heavy modification to be as enjoyable as it could be. I've also run it twice with heavy modification and enjoyed the hell out of the resulting chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>True - though there's something of a tonal disssonance from what is supposed to be the &quot;typical&quot; V5 game in a number of elements, the adventure has some quite engrossing imagery and I agree it can be made quite entertaining for ST and players both with some strategic tweaking.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Not that i'm doing any such a thing anytime soon, considering my current game is more of a gonzo melange of Bloodlines, Redemption, BJD and some random bits from multiple editions &amp; media, V5 comic included. Hard to make a Salubri warrior-nun fresh out of torpor, a bride of Dracula with a cursed sword, a Caitiff that recently discovered his Cappadocian origins - after ganking Prince Lacroix, a Gangrel &quot;cured&quot; of his Gargoyle condition by the blessings of a cabbie driver in a chance encounter in LA and some other not <i>quite </i>as extreme weirdoes fit in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> Your suggestions on how to deal with it are fairly good, to which i would only add expanding somewhat the cast of NPCs, to give more of a sense of scale and dramatic loss to the total meltdown of the city's kindred society.<br /> <br /> Combing the adventure itself should be helpful, specially if one crosschecks with the wiki or their own books for some morsels and references, what together with purloining a number from other books like &quot;London by Night&quot; (for Victorian Age Vampire), Blood &amp; Fire and the Sun Has Set (Giovanni Chronicles 2 &amp; 3) and a World of Darkness (1st or 2nd edition, if you have both, even better) could expand your list of figures for the PCs to meet, interact &amp;/or witness the capture or destruction to almost Chicago by Night proportions and offer lots for them to do outside of the main path of the Horcruxes hunt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528928-opinion-the-fall-of-london-is-a-great-adventure-but-you-need-to-use-only-70-of-it?p=1528942#post1528942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could work on why my player character might go back to London after a 100+ years of absence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In a partly broken post-SI strike London, a powerful ancilla or elder (which one he can claim to be will depend on how much of the old guard has fallen) with past ties returning after a long hiatus could make a compromise candidate for primogen or even prince, depending on circunstances and who might support it for the sake of blocking someone else.<br /> <br /> Damn, such a kindred having to deal with an unexpected rocket-boosted rise to the top due to being a prop/paper tiger strongly dependent on stronger &amp; far better informed mentors/allies/patrons can be quite the challenge on itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-04-2024, 02:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T11:37:41-08:00","id":1529024,"title":"","content":"A good idea, and my Malkavian would be reeling from the changes in his fortune and he has a good place in his current city and I would have to work out in the story how much of the old guard is left and if a servant of Mithras might make an appearance as my character is rightfully scared of the ancient monster and the rampage he went on when he didn't like what Valerius did in his place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T19:06:15-08:00","id":1530418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528928-opinion-the-fall-of-london-is-a-great-adventure-but-you-need-to-use-only-70-of-it?p=1529024#post1529024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A good idea, and my Malkavian would be reeling from the changes in his fortune and he has a good place in his current city and I would have to work out in the story how much of the old guard is left and if a servant of Mithras might make an appearance as my character is rightfully scared of the ancient monster and the rampage he went on when he didn't like what Valerius did in his place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hope he has some relatively reliable childer, pupils and allies to bring along on this ride, because it's sure to be bumpy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T11:08:12-08:00","id":1530569,"title":"","content":"Childer no, but he does have some strong alliances to help him out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 202